@startuml
title TLS Handshake — Full Client/Server Message Flow

participant Client
participant Server

== 1. Hello: negotiate version & cipher ==

Client -> Server: ClientHello\n(supported TLS versions, cipher suites, ClientRandom)

Server -> Client: ServerHello\n(chosen TLS version, chosen cipher suite, ServerRandom)

== 2. Server proves its identity ==

Server -> Client: Certificate\n(Leaf cert [contains Server PUBLIC key] + Intermediate CA cert)

Server -> Client: ServerKeyExchange\n(ephemeral ECDHE public key,\nSIGNED with Server's PRIVATE key)

Server -> Client: ServerHelloDone

note right of Client
**Check leaf certificate (public key check):**
1. Walk chain: Leaf -> Intermediate -> Root CA
2. Verify each signature using issuer's public key
3. Root CA must be in local Truststore
4. Check validity dates (not expired)
5. Check hostname matches SAN
6. Check EKU = serverAuth
end note

Client -> Client: Verify ServerKeyExchange signature\nusing PUBLIC key extracted from leaf cert

note right of Client
**This is the "challenge":**
Signature only validates if it was produced
by the PRIVATE key matching the leaf cert's
public key. Proves Server really owns
the identity in the certificate.
end note

== 3. Key exchange ==

Client -> Server: ClientKeyExchange\n(Client's ephemeral ECDHE public key)

Client -> Client: Compute Pre-Master Secret\n(ECDH: own private key + Server's public key)
Server -> Server: Compute Pre-Master Secret\n(ECDH: own private key + Client's public key)

note over Client, Server
Both sides now derive the same
**Master Secret** = PRF(PreMasterSecret, ClientRandom, ServerRandom)
then derive symmetric **Session Keys**
(encryption key + MAC key) from it.
end note

== 4. Confirm handshake (mutual proof) ==

Client -> Server: ChangeCipherSpec
Client -> Server: Finished\n(hash of all handshake messages,\nencrypted with new session key)

Server -> Server: Verify Client's Finished message

Server -> Client: ChangeCipherSpec
Server -> Client: Finished\n(hash of all handshake messages,\nencrypted with new session key)

Client -> Client: Verify Server's Finished message

note over Client, Server
Both sides confirmed they derived
the identical session key.
Handshake complete.
end note

== 5. Application data ==

Client -> Server: Encrypted Application Data\n(symmetric session key)
Server -> Client: Encrypted Application Data\n(symmetric session key)

@enduml
